    "word_count": 50,
    "html": "<p>Sheikh Rashid bin Humaid Al Nuaimi is an Emirati businessman and a son of Ajman’s ruler. He founded R Holding, whose interests span property, hotels and education, and owns construction group Tech. A business administration graduate of the American University of Sharjah, he also chairs Ajman’s Municipality and Planning Department.</p>\r\n"
  },
  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "As president of the UAE Football Association, Sheikh Rashid bin Humaid Al Nuaimi backed a development programme extending from grassroots participation to the national team. His interest included beach soccer: he called for regular competitions involving clubs and institutional teams to increase the number of players and widen access to organised competition.\n\nHe also supported athletes in education. At the American University of Sharjah, he agreed to endow a scholarship for students combining strong academic results with sporting ability. The programme addresses financial need as well as performance, helping eligible students pursue university study while continuing their sport.",
