    "word_count": 98,
    "html": "<p>As president of the UAE Football Association, Sheikh Rashid bin Humaid Al Nuaimi backed a development programme extending from grassroots participation to the national team. His interest included beach soccer: he called for regular competitions involving clubs and institutional teams to increase the number of players and widen access to organised competition.</p>\r\n<p>He also supported athletes in education. At the American University of Sharjah, he agreed to endow a scholarship for students combining strong academic results with sporting ability. The programme addresses financial need as well as performance, helping eligible students pursue university study while continuing their sport.</p>\r\n"
  },
